./manual/CHANGESLOG.md:2738:### 2026-05-29 - Feature: SlicePro Extended Sync — per-slice beat sync beyond 512 lines
./manual/CHANGESLOG.md:2740:SlicePro now optionally pushes slices (and the root sample) past Renoise's 512 `beat_sync_lines` cap so long-form sliced material stays tempo-locked far beyond what the native UI allows. When **Extended sync** is enabled, any slice whose musical length works out to more than 512 lines is injected with its true value through the BeatSyncHack XRNI roundtrip instead of being silently clamped to 512. All over-512 slices in an instrument are injected in a **single** save/reload pass (not one reload per slice), and the injection runs after every other per-slice property is set, so mute group, NNA, loop mode, autofade, oneshot and beat sync mode are all preserved. The extended values exist only at runtime — saving the song stays crash-safe (see the BeatSyncHack save protection below). Default is OFF. macOS/Linux only (uses shell `zip`/`unzip`). Toggle via the new "Extended sync >512 (runtime only, XRNS-safe)" checkbox in the SlicePro dialog, or the `SliceProExtendedSync` preference. When disabled, behavior is unchanged (clamp to 512 with a warning).
./manual/CHANGESLOG.md:2744:Two reliability upgrades to the BeatSyncHack save protection. (1) **Reload restoration:** the list of samples using extended (>512) BeatSyncLines is now stored inside the song as legal restoration metadata (`renoise.song().tool_data`, written during `app_will_save_document_observable`). When the project is reopened, the metadata is read and the extended values are re-applied automatically on a one-shot idle tick — previously, hacked values were lost on reload and had to be re-applied by hand. The illegal value itself is never written to a song property; only the recipe to rebuild it persists. (2) **Batch roundtrip:** restoration after save now groups hacked samples by instrument and re-injects each instrument in one XRNI save/reload instead of one reload per sample, and surfaces failures explicitly (`restored N, FAILED M — re-apply manually`) instead of leaving a sample silently clamped. A new global `pakettiBeatSyncHackRoundtrip(instrument_index, {[sample_index]=lines, ...})` is the shared core used by the dialog presets, the SlicePro extended-sync path, the after-save restore, and the after-reload restore. The save-time clamp-to-512 (which keeps the XRNS crash-safe) is unchanged.
