./manual/CHANGESLOG.md:3048:Disabling a context (e.g. Mixer, Pattern Editor, Sample Editor) in `Main Menu:Options:Paketti Menu Configuration` now actually skips registering those menu entries at boot, including the ~2,390 entries that call `renoise.tool():add_menu_entry{...}` directly instead of going through the `PakettiAddMenuEntry` helper. Previously only the ~860 helper-routed entries honored the per-context preference; the remaining 2,390 direct calls were always queued, sorted, and registered regardless of the toggle — so disabling a category never made reloads faster.
